# Against All Odds

Against All Odds is a statistics capstone project focused on predicting professional sports outcomes while also evaluating how reliable or fragile each prediction may be.

## Main Research Question

Can pre-game statistical information be used to predict professional sports outcomes while also identifying which predictions are reliable, fragile, or unusually vulnerable to an upset?

## Project Timeline

August 29, 2026 – December 3, 2026

## Required Sports

- NBA
- NFL
- Premier League

## Optional Extensions

- La Liga
- Bundesliga
- Serie A
- Ligue 1

## Prediction Reliability Categories

The project will eventually classify predictions into three categories:

- **Predict** — prediction is considered sufficiently reliable
- **Caution** — prediction has meaningful uncertainty or fragility
- **Abstain** — available information does not support a reliable prediction

Final definitions and thresholds will be determined through model validation rather than arbitrary cutoffs.

